# Trivy accepted exceptions (task A09). CRITICAL findings block CI.
#
# One ID per line. Add an entry only with a reason, a date and Person B's approval
# in the pull request, for example:
#   # 2026-10-01 no fix released; not reachable from our code; approved by <name> in #<PR>
#   CVE-2026-00000
# 2026-10-10 zlib1g in the Debian 12 base of node:24.13.0-bookworm-slim (sdlc-api, sdlc-worker,
# sdlc-runner; release scan of V04, design/ADR-M66 §2.6): Debian marks it "will not fix". The flaw
# is in minizip (zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6), which Debian ships apart (libminizip1), not in zlib1g;
# no platform image installs minizip. Remove when Debian 12 ships a fix or the base moves on.
# Approved by Harry (Person B) in PR #276.
CVE-2023-45853
# 2026-10-26 Go stdlib 1.24.11 in /usr/local/bin/gitleaks of sdlc-runner (Gitleaks 8.30.1, the
# latest release; task H04, design/ADR-M93; found by the release scan of V15 on PR #449): the flaw
# is in crypto/tls session resumption (fixed in Go 1.24.13 and 1.25.7). The runner runs Gitleaks
# only as `gitleaks dir` on a local folder, with a clean environment and its own configuration
# file (secrets.ts); Gitleaks opens no TLS connection there. Remove when a Gitleaks release is
# built with a fixed Go, and update platform/deploy/scripts/gitleaks.sh and ci.yml together.
# Approved by Harry (Person B) in PR #449 (2026-10-26).
CVE-2025-68121
